00:59:34,000 --> 00:59:38,000
And to get it more precise, it's the standard deviation

1149
00:59:38,000 --> 00:59:44,000
of the S&P 500 stock price index for one month,

1150
00:59:44,000 --> 00:59:46,000
multiplied by the square root of 1.

1151
00:59:46,000 --> 00:59:47,500
And the S&P 500 stock

1152
00:59:47,500 --> 00:59:49,000
price index is the standard deviation

1153
00:59:49,000 --> 00:59:51,000
of the S&P 500 stock price index for one month,

1154
00:59:51,000 --> 00:59:53,000
