01:09:05,000 --> 01:09:09,000
So, this leads me to think that

1335
01:09:09,000 --> 01:09:13,000
option pricing theory, I've presented a theory.

1336
01:09:13,000 --> 01:09:16,000
The black shoals theory is very

1337
01:09:16,000 --> 01:09:19,000
elegant and a very useful tool.

1338
01:09:19,000 --> 01:09:23,000
Especially useful when things behave normally.

1339
01:09:23,000 --> 01:09:27,500
But I think one always has to keep in the back of

1340
01:09:27,500 --> 01:09:32,000
one's mind the risk of sudden major changes like we've seen here.

1341
01:09:32,000 --> 01:09:34,000
So, let me just give a quick summary.

1342
01:09:34,000 --> 01:09:38,000
So, let me just give some final thoughts about options.

1343
01:09:38,000 --> 01:09:42,000
I launched this lecture by saying they're very important.

1344
01:09:42,000 --> 01:09:52,000
And they affect our lives in many ways.

1345
01:09:52,000 --> 01:09:55,000
I've been trying to campaign for

1346
01:09:55,000 --> 01:09:58,000
the expansion of our financial markets.

1347
01:09:58,000 --> 01:10:00,500
Working with my colleagues

1348
01:10:00,500 --> 01:10:03,000
and the Chicago Mercantile Exchange,

1349
01:10:03,000 --> 01:10:06,500
we launched options in 2006 on

1350
01:10:06,500 --> 01:10:10,000
single-family homes in the United States.

1351
01:10:10,000 --> 01:10:13,000
We were hoping that people would buy put

1352
01:10:13,000 --> 01:10:16,000
options to protect themselves against home price declines.

1353
01:10:16,000 --> 01:10:21,000
But the market never took off.

1354
01:10:21,000 --> 01:10:26,000
We have since seen huge human suffering because of the

1355
01:10:26,000 --> 01:10:31,000
failure of people to protect themselves against home price declines.

1356
01:10:31,000 --> 01:10:32,000
There are things.

1357
01:10:32,000 --> 01:10:35,500
Various noises that were made by people in

1358
01:10:35,500 --> 01:10:39,000
power that suggested that maybe something could be done.

1359
01:10:39,000 --> 01:10:42,000
President Obama proposed something

1360
01:10:42,000 --> 01:10:45,000
called Home Price Protection Program.

1361
01:10:45,000 --> 01:10:48,000
And it sounded like an option, a put option program.

1362
01:10:48,000 --> 01:10:49,500
But actually, it was a

1363
01:10:49,500 --> 01:10:51,000
much more subtle program than that.

1364
01:10:51,000 --> 01:10:56,000
It was a program to incentivize mortgage originators to

1365
01:10:56,000 --> 01:11:01,000
do workouts on mortgages if the mortgages would default.

1366
01:11:02,000 --> 01:11:04,000
If home prices were to fall.

1367
01:11:04,000 --> 01:11:06,000
And nothing really happened with it.

1368
01:11:06,000 --> 01:11:09,000
The President can't get things started either, always.

1369
01:11:09,000 --> 01:11:12,000
I've been proposing that mortgages should have

1370
01:11:12,000 --> 01:11:15,000
put options on the house attached to them.

1371
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:17,000
When you buy a house, get a

1372
01:11:17,000 --> 01:11:19,000
mortgage, you should automatically get a put option.

1373
01:11:19,000 --> 01:11:21,000
I've got a new paper on that.

1374
01:11:21,000 --> 01:11:24,000
But these are kind of futuristic things at the moment.

1375
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:27,000
But my sense, I'm just saying this at

1376
01:11:27,000 --> 01:11:30,000
the end just to try to impress on you

1377
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:31,000
what I think is the real future of mortgage.

1378
01:11:32,000 --> 01:11:36,000
What I think is the real importance of options markets.

1379
01:11:36,000 --> 01:11:40,000
People don't manage risks well in the present world.

1380
01:11:40,000 --> 01:11:44,000
Having options or insurance-like contracts of an expanded

1381
01:11:44,000 --> 01:11:48,000
nature will help people manage their risks better.

1382
01:11:48,000 --> 01:11:52,000
And it will make for a better world.

1383
01:11:52,000 --> 01:11:56,000
Okay, I'll see you on Monday.

